From 736011ec5102247a2dea9cc47b8d41a32de6ce42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KavoPDF prototype <proto@local>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 02:42:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] prototype(route c): a two-column band as one tabbed paragraph
 per baseline

A page set in columns is written as one anchored DrawingML text box per line,
because the column pass emits one block per line and the two columns' lines
interleave in y: flowed column-by-column the right column lands below the left
column's last line, and the gap needed is NEGATIVE, which place() cannot
express. Google Docs rasterises anchored boxes on import, which is the 81-92 %
SSIM the pixel score reports.

This routes a column band through the construct flowRow already uses for a form
row: one paragraph per BASELINE, with a tab stop at each column's measured x.
That makes the flow's sequence equal the page's y sequence, so no line is ever
above the flow and no gap is negative.

  columnRowBlocks()   - a page's blocks with each run of column lines re-cut
  columnLineHome()    - is this block one line of one column
  taggedColumnEdges() - column left edges from the column pass's tags
  columnRowsOfRun()   - the run, flattened to boxes, grouped by baseline
  copyBoxAt()         - one field of a row, moved onto the row's baseline
  COLUMN_ROWS / p2w.colrows - the flag, on by default

Measured on the 213-document corpus, LibreOffice render against the source PDF:
text-box anchors 1037 -> 836; wp:anchor 13211 -> 13010; page counts unchanged
on all 20 documents whose bytes changed; zero-gap lines 0 on every converted
document (policy-2col 1 -> 0, 69_two_col 2 -> 0, 66_two_col 7 -> 0).
policy-2col-spanning-section-heading 62 -> 2 text boxes, median |dy| 0.02 pt,
max |dy| 0.08 -> 0.02; 69_two_col_legal_numbered_clauses 36 -> 7.

NOT MERGED. Prototype branch only.
